From: MCC45TR <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: reject firmware boot errors before enabling commands

The common boot loop treats any nonzero status as completion. An invalid
UC-region status logs an error and breaks into the success path; fatal,
fence and pending-only statuses also proceed without a ready indication.

Check the existing error mask before ready, return -EIO on errors and
continue bounded polling until the ready bit is present. Preserve the
existing timeout and both callers' firmware/power unwind paths. Compare
the Iris33 boot status contract against OnePlus SM7675 source revision
1138e00fee63582a0cc6a53af3286621786827b7, variant/iris33.

This inactive candidate does not enable an OF match or execute firmware.

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_common.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_common.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_common.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_common.c
@@ -80,12 +80,14 @@ int iris_vpu_boot_firmware(struct iris_core *core)
 	writel(ctrl_init, core->reg_base + CTRL_INIT);
 	writel(0x1, core->reg_base + CPU_CS_SCIACMDARG3);
 
-	while (!ctrl_status && count < max_tries) {
+	while (count < max_tries) {
 		ctrl_status = readl(core->reg_base + CTRL_STATUS);
-		if ((ctrl_status & CTRL_ERROR_STATUS__M) == 0x4) {
-			dev_err(core->dev, "invalid setting for uc_region\n");
-			break;
+		if (ctrl_status & CTRL_ERROR_STATUS__M) {
+			dev_err(core->dev, "firmware boot failed: status %#x\n", ctrl_status);
+			return -EIO;
 		}
+		if (ctrl_status & BIT(0))
+			break;
 
 		usleep_range(50, 100);
 		count++;
